{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Crisis at the Restaurant", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Figuring It Out", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Perfect Infinitives to Express Deduction and Disbelief", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Perfect Infinitives with modals <span class=\"italic\">must, might, could, may</span> and <span class=\"italic\">can't</span> to express a deduction or disbelief about something in the present or the past.  <br>The modal you choose depends on the level of probability you want to express.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">must</span></span> for logical conclusions. There is a strong degree of certainty about the present situation. <br> <br>You use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">may, might</span></span> and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">could</span></span> to express a deduction about things in the present or the past when there are other possibilities or when the situation is possible but not certain. These modals have the same meaning. <br> <br>You use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">can't</span></span> when the situation is impossible or to express disbelief. <br> <br>Structure: <br>modal verb + have + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": " You might have felt underappreciated in the past.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The last few weeks may have been the most difficult I've ever had since I began here. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Purpose", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use purpose clauses to express the reasons for an action, or the intended motive of a specific situation. <br>You use words like <span class=\"italic\">to, in order to, so as to</span> or <span class=\"italic\">for + -ing</span> to introduce a purpose clause.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Purpose clauses are subordinate to the main clause. The order of the clauses can be interchangeable, as long as the relationship between the two remains clear. <br>Example: <br><span class=\"italic\">I have come up with a new plan <span class=\"strong\">in order to</span> stay focused.</span> <br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">In order to</span> stay focused, I have come up with a new plan.</span> <br> <br>You use <span class=\"italic\">to</span> with an infinitive as a way to express purpose. We refer to this structure as an Infinitive of purpose. <br>Example: <br><span class=\"italic\">I called <span class=\"strong\">to</span> find out if the order had been shipped.</span> <br> <br>You use <span class=\"italic\">in order to</span> or <span class=\"italic\">so as to</span> to emphasize an intention or a necessity. <br>Example:  <br><span class=\"italic\">I would like to call for a meeting <span class=\"strong\">in order to / so as to</span> address the current issues in the restaurant.</span> <br> <br>You use <span class=\"italic\">in order that</span> or <span class=\"italic\">so that</span> when the second clause starts with a pronoun or a noun. <br>Example: <br><span class=\"italic\">You need to give me an answer, <span class=\"strong\">so that / in order that</span> I can address the problem quickly.</span> <br> <br>You also use <span class=\"italic\">for + verb -ing</span> to express purpose and intended use. <br>Example: <br><span class=\"italic\">These boots are made <span class=\"strong\">for walking.</span></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I've called you here <span class=\"strong\">with the hopes of making</span> you all more motivated and happier working here. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">I'm determined to</span> keep you employed here.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "So I am wondering how you feel about me hiring another server in order <span class=\"strong\">to</span> allow each of you a few less hours a week or <span class=\"strong\">to</span> help out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When you want to express purpose and intention, the following words and expressions can be used. <br> <ul><li>Verbs <br><span class=\"italic\">I mean/plan/intend/aim/hope to ...</span></li> <li>Nouns <br><span class=\"italic\">My goal/intention/dream/purpose/hope/aim is to ...</span> </li> <li>Adjectives<br><span class=\"italic\">I'm eager/determined/resolved/tempted to ...</span> </li> <li>Nouns/Verbal phrases <br><span class=\"italic\">To have +  high hopes of / no intention of / no thoughts of / half a mind to ...</span> <br><span class=\"italic\">To be + / toying with the idea ...</span> </li> <li>Prepositional phrases <br><span class=\"italic\">in the hopes of getting / with a view to getting / with the aim of getting ...</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rough ride ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a difficult time ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We've had a rough ride lately.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about customer relations.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "peak hours ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the busiest time of day ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: With my goal to offer superior customer service, another server at peak hours will help us achieve that. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "juiced ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having too much work ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  She can act as a floater who can help you whenever you feel juiced.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "floater ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who helps with various tasks ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She can act as a floater who can help you whenever you feel juiced.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to transpire ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to happen ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Tell what actually transpired between them. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob10aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "a true reflection ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an honest representation ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What he said is not a true reflection of how he feels.   ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "impetus", "type": "name"}, {"content": "motivation ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I don't think it was a true reflection of what actually transpired, but it may have been the impetus to bring me to this point.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob10aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "going forward ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "from now on ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I worked out a plan with Bill that'll give you each two weeks' paid vacation every year going forward.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob10aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "If you have a job, write down ideas about how it could be better. If you don't have a job, make a description of a perfect job.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell a friend what would make this job ideal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a wish list of the things you would like to have at work. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Back up each wish with a reason for that wish.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share and compare your wishes with your friends' wishes.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I tell a friend about the perfect job.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a wish list.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about the reasons for my wishes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share and compare wishes with other friends.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type